 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same collection is also served on a machine-readable companion route for programmatic consumers `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Both surfaces can be filtered to a single specialty. Given a specialty, the directory page and the machine-readable route each present only the veterinarians who hold it, and the page still lists its results a page at a time `[REQ-VET-003]`. The match is on the whole specialty name and disregards letter case — a value matching only the start of a name matches no veterinarian. A specialty naming no veterinarian returns the ordinary page or document with no veterinarians rather than an error, and a blank or spaces-only value filters nothing, exactly as an empty owner search does. With no specialty given, each surface behaves as it does without the filter `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by one or more veterinarians, when the directory page is opened filtered to that specialty, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by one or more veterinarians, when the machine-readable route is requested filtered to that specialty, then only those veterinarians are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty differing from a held one only by letter case, when either surface is filtered to it, then it matches.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty, when either surface is requested, then it behaves as it does without the filter.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. The machine-readable companion route returns the same veterinarians as the page, in a form for programmatic consumers; it is a supported surface under `REQ-VET-003`, and it accepts the specialty filter on the same terms as the page.
+3. A value matching only the start of a specialty name matches no veterinarian — the filter is on the whole name, not a prefix.
+4. A specialty naming no veterinarian returns the ordinary page or machine-readable document with no veterinarians, as a successful response rather than an error, on both surfaces.
+5. A blank or spaces-only specialty value filters nothing and returns the same result as omitting the filter, on both surfaces.
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
